  "notes": "Sync->async refactor of NotebookLMClient and the MCP tool handlers. The workload points the client's BASE_URL and BATCHEXECUTE_URL at a fake NotebookLM server on localhost (background thread, stand-in for external I/O only) and awaits any coroutine a call returns, so one script runs on both versions. It runs 250 rounds of client calls (list/get/create/rename, summaries, source text, query plus follow-up, conversation history) and 20 rounds of about 35 server tool calls via FastMCP .fn with server._client set. Digests match. Base 4.8 s, head 6.3 s; coverage 85% base, 60% head. Most uncovered head lines are the new query_stream / notebook_query_stream code, which doesn't exist in base. A few tools return handled errors because the fake server gives generic responses; they are the same on both versions. Head's async client makes one request at a time here, nothing runs concurrently."
 },
